+### remote_realtime
+
+**Type:** Boolean
+**Default:** `false`
+**Required:** No
+
+Stream audio to a [NeMo-Speech](https://github.com/NVIDIA/NeMo-Speech.cpp) server (`nemo-speech serve`) over its realtime WebSocket and type words at the cursor while you speak. Needs `mode = "remote"`. Audio goes to `<remote_endpoint>/v1/audio/transcriptions/realtime` (`http` becomes `ws`, `https` becomes `wss`). Typing at the cursor while the hotkey is held confuses some compositors, so push-to-talk is promoted to toggle, the same as for the other streaming engines.
+
+A word is typed once the next word has started, because the server can still extend the last word and attach punctuation to it. A word that could begin a multi-word replacement (see `vocabulary_files` and `[text] replacements`) waits until the phrase completes or fails. When you stop, the server's final transcript is compared with what was typed: missing words are appended and a word that really differs is backspaced and retyped. `[text]` replacements, filler-word removal and spoken punctuation apply to streamed text.
+
+If the server is unreachable or fails mid-recording, voxtype shows a notification and keeps the words typed so far. Code that transcribes a finished recording instead of streaming it posts the audio to `/v1/audio/transcriptions` with the same vocabulary.
+
+**Example:**
+```toml
+[whisper]
+mode = "remote"
+remote_endpoint = "http://127.0.0.1:8010"
+remote_realtime = true
+
+[hotkey]
+mode = "toggle"
+```
+
+### vocabulary_files
+
+**Type:** Array of strings
+**Default:** `[]`
+**Required:** No
+
+Vocabulary files for `remote_realtime`, read again at the start of every recording, so an edit applies the next time you start dictating. Later files override earlier ones for the same left-hand side. A missing file is skipped without a message. A leading `~` expands to `$HOME`.
+
+One entry per line, UTF-8. A line starting with `#` is a comment; blank lines are ignored.
+
+```text
+# A term to boost
+Nextcloud
+# A correction: whole-word, case-insensitive. "Nextcloud" is boosted too.
+next cloud => Nextcloud
+```
+
+Boosted terms go to the server as `speech_contexts`. At most 256 phrases are sent; the log says when a list is truncated.
+
+**Example:**
+```toml
+[whisper]
+vocabulary_files = ["/etc/voxtype/vocabulary.txt", "~/.config/voxtype/vocabulary.txt"]
+```
+
+### remote_boost
+
+**Type:** Float
+**Default:** `2.5`
+**Required:** No
+
+Boost score sent with the vocabulary terms. NeMo-Speech's cache-aware RNNT decoder clamps it to 5.0, so voxtype clamps it too; 2 to 3 is typical. `0` turns boosting off while keeping corrections.
+
 ### whisper_cli_path
 
